Z||000005||Philphine||12-30-2000||12:16 PM||||kinda pointless on a stock fiero since the handle is lined up with the ribbing that goes around the car. you'd either need to get rid of all the ribbing or leave the handle there and for some reason make it useless. if you just like tricky electronic stuff it would be better to leave the handle and have the electric option.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||12-30-2000||01:12 PM||||If you eliminate the handle you'd need to fill the hole and splice pieces of door trim to be long enough to cover the blank area. This won't be a whole lot of fun. that trim is made from somekind of polyethylene or a relative that's going to be tough to splice and not end up with obvious seems.<P>On the older trim the end result won't look a whole lot diferant than it does now. On the newer round trim it should make for a little better line. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slick781||12-30-2000||05:57 PM||||thanx guys, just something i had thought about.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroJoe||12-30-2000||10:06 PM||||I saw once in a low rider magazine a kit you could get for shaved door handles.  It included a solenoid to pop the latch, and then a hydraulic piston (optional) to actually open the door for you.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mshill||12-30-2000||10:37 PM||||My F-50 kit will have mechanical buttons, but there is no place for a mechanical lock.  The electonic locking is cheap and easy to install, but I also wondered about if you locked your keys in the car or the battery died?  Do slim-jims work on Fieros?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||12-31-2000||12:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TheFiero64:<BR><B>What would you do if the system stops working and you can't get in or your batt dies?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>for a emergency back up, you could run a cable from latch, thru front doorjam into the inside rear part of front wheelwell. sorta like they do for cars with electric gas cap release. Just keep it a secret where its at.<P>||||reg||1
